Subject: [PATCH] [mlir][bufferization] Tensor-likeness per instance; bridges
 checked by their interface alone

`TensorLikeType` and `BufferLikeType` belong to a type's class, so a
type whose instances are tensor-like for some parameters alone (a
wrapper of another type, tensor-like where the wrapped type is, and not
where it wraps a scalar) cannot implement them: every instance would be
a tensor to One-Shot Bufferize. Interfaces already decide per instance
through `extraClassOf`, as `SymbolOpInterface` does for ops; the two
bufferization type interfaces now do: `isTensorLike()` and
`isBufferLike()`, true by default, narrow `isa` to the instances that
answer true.

`bufferization.to_tensor` and `to_buffer` also carry
`SameOperandsAndResultShape` and `SameOperandsAndResultElementType`,
which require shaped types, beside
`Bufferization_TensorAndBufferMatch`, which asks the tensor-like type
whether the buffer type is compatible
(`TensorLikeType::verifyCompatibleBufferType`). For builtins that check
is the same shapes and element types; for a tensor-like type that is not
shaped, the two traits refuse every bridge. They go, and the interface's
check is the one rule.
---
diff --git a/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Bufferization/IR/BufferizationOps.td b/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Bufferization/IR/BufferizationOps.td
index 30317c2d..e95dc992 100644
--- a/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Bufferization/IR/BufferizationOps.td
+++ b/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Bufferization/IR/BufferizationOps.td
@@ -329,8 +329,6 @@ class Bufferization_TensorAndBufferMatch<string tensor, string buffer> : PredOpT
 >;
 
 def Bufferization_ToTensorOp : Bufferization_Op<"to_tensor", [
-    SameOperandsAndResultShape,
-    SameOperandsAndResultElementType,
     Bufferization_TensorAndBufferMatch<"result", "buffer">
   ]> {
   let summary = "create a tensor-like type from a buffer-like type";
@@ -413,8 +411,6 @@ def Bufferization_ToTensorOp : Bufferization_Op<"to_tensor", [
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 
 def Bufferization_ToBufferOp : Bufferization_Op<"to_buffer", [
-    SameOperandsAndResultShape,
-    SameOperandsAndResultElementType,
     Pure,
     Bufferization_TensorAndBufferMatch<"tensor", "buffer">
   ]> {
diff --git a/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Bufferization/IR/BufferizationTypeInterfaces.td b/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Bufferization/IR/BufferizationTypeInterfaces.td
index 6bbc6cb5..cd97664c 100644
--- a/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Bufferization/IR/BufferizationTypeInterfaces.td
+++ b/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Bufferization/IR/BufferizationTypeInterfaces.td
@@ -33,8 +33,25 @@ def Bufferization_TensorLikeTypeInterface
       /*args=*/(ins
         "::mlir::bufferization::BufferLikeType":$bufferType,
         "::llvm::function_ref<::mlir::InFlightDiagnostic()>":$emitError)
+    >,
+    InterfaceMethod<[{
+        Returns whether this instance of the type is tensor-like. A type whose
+        instances are tensor-like for some parameters alone (a wrapper of
+        another type, tensor-like where the wrapped type is) implements the
+        interface and answers per instance; `isa<TensorLikeType>` is false
+        for an instance that answers false.
+      }],
+      /*retTy=*/"bool",
+      /*methodName=*/"isTensorLike",
+      /*args=*/(ins),
+      /*methodBody=*/"",
+      /*defaultImplementation=*/[{ return true; }]
     >
   ];
+
+  let extraClassOf = [{
+    return $_type.isTensorLike();
+  }];
 }
 
 def Bufferization_BufferLikeTypeInterface
@@ -44,8 +61,27 @@ def Bufferization_BufferLikeTypeInterface
     Indicates that this type is a buffer type (similarly to a MLIR builtin
     memref) for bufferization purposes.
 
-    The interface currently has no methods as it is used by types to opt into
-    being supported by the bufferization procedures.
+    A type opts into being supported by the bufferization procedures by
+    implementing it.
+  }];
+
+  let methods = [
+    InterfaceMethod<[{
+        Returns whether this instance of the type is buffer-like. A type whose
+        instances are buffer-like for some parameters alone answers per
+        instance; `isa<BufferLikeType>` is false for an instance that answers
+        false.
+      }],
+      /*retTy=*/"bool",
+      /*methodName=*/"isBufferLike",
+      /*args=*/(ins),
+      /*methodBody=*/"",
+      /*defaultImplementation=*/[{ return true; }]
+    >
+  ];
+
+  let extraClassOf = [{
+    return $_type.isBufferLike();
   }];
 }
 
